                "In summer (May/June), the STWJ abruptly shifts NORTH of Tibet; this sudden northward jump triggers the 'Burst of Monsoon' over India.",
                "Tibetan Plateau (average altitude 4,500 m) acts as an elevated thermal heat engine, generating the Tropical Easterly Jet (TEJ / Somali Jet) at 150 hPa.",
                "The TEJ descends over the Mascarene High (southern Indian Ocean), intensifying the cross-equatorial monsoon surge towards India."
